// c19_widen_call_unary: the public->`secret` (ADR 0019 D5) and public->`?T` (ADR
// 0014 D3) WIDENINGS, over the two expression shapes `scg` used to skip.
//
// WHAT IT PINS. A widened binding wraps its right-hand side — `snc types` prints
// `(widen-secret … :secret i64)` / `(widen-null … :?bool)`, and `snc mir` emits a
// whole `(vN:?T opaque vM)` for it. `scg` applied that for a LITERAL or a plain
// VARIABLE right-hand side but not for a CALL or a UNARY one, because the
// `Expr::Call` and `Expr::Unary` dispatch arms handed their output straight to
// `out` instead of building a temp and splicing the wrapper in front (the node's
// type is known only after its children synthesize, so the wrapper cannot be
// written first). `dump_te_binary` had always done it correctly, which is what
// made the omission survive: `let x: ?i64 = a + 1;` was fine.
//
// The four cells below are {call, unary} x {secret, nullable} — the whole matrix
// for THIS position and THESE two shapes, which is narrower than it sounds:
//   `s`   CALL  -> secret     `n`   CALL  -> nullable
//   `sm`  UNARY -> secret     `opt` UNARY -> nullable
// Sibling arms still drop the same wrapper (`let v: secret i64 = p.x;`,
// `= a[0];`, `= declassify(s);` …) and are tracked separately — see the SCOPE
// comment on the `Expr::Unary` arm in `selfhost/types/borrow.sentinel` for the
// full list and the repros.
//
// WHY IT WAS INVISIBLE — and the answer is NOT that the corpus avoids the shape.
// Real code writes it: `let p0: secret u8 = i64_to_u8(76);` appears 18 times —
// 16 in `examples/security/chacha20_stream.sentinel` (two per line, p0..p15),
// 1 in `chacha20poly1305.sentinel`, 1 in
// `sentinel_library/std/security/aead.sentinel` — because `i64_to_u8` is a
// BUILTIN returning public `u8`. On a pre-fix binary those emit
// `(let #0 secret u8 (call #6 …))` against the oracle's
// `(widen-secret (call #6 …) :secret u8)`.
// They were never COMPARED. The semantic stage oracles do no module discovery, so
// the direct form of all three dies on `use` imports are not yet wired; and the
// merged form — the only other way in — dies in `snc merge`'s Bar-A printer on
// `expression `cast` is out of Bar-A scope`. Both exclusions are structural, not
// accidental, which is why every differential stayed green while the gap sat
// there, and is the sharpest argument yet for widening that printer (the open
// menu's item 5): it would take the semantic sweeps from 11 real programs to
// ~100 and pull these three in.
// The MIR half was the nastier one: a dropped `opaque` SHIFTS EVERY LATER VALUE
// NUMBER in the block, so the diff would have looked nothing like its cause.
//
// Unlike the other recent mirror fixtures this one reaches the CODEGEN
// differential too — no `f64`, `ptr` or reserved-name intrinsic makes the oracle
// bail — so it pins the `cg_widen` path (`{ i1 1, <op> }` for a `?T`) as well as
// the two dumps.
//
// 42 + (-21) + 20 + 1 = 42.

fn half(x: i64) -> i64 {
    x / 2
}

fn main() -> i64 {
    // CALL right-hand side, widened to `secret i64` and to `?i64`.
    let s: secret i64 = half(84);
    let n: ?i64 = half(40);
    // UNARY right-hand side, widened to `?bool` and to `secret i64`.
    let flag: bool = false;
    let opt: ?bool = !flag;
    let m: i64 = 21;
    let sm: secret i64 = -m;
    if unwrap_or(opt, false) {
        declassify(s) + declassify(sm) + unwrap_or(n, 0) + 1
    } else {
        0
    }
}
